From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: the shared-round era (prof, draws, costs, fills, segments)

ai-engine 32060d706 grafted onto the pin stack: the shared-round knob family that the
later GLM levers ride on. It adds cuda_engine_ovn.zig (the load-time knob opens),
cuda_engine_prof.zig, cuda_draw1.zig, cuda_cost_time.zig, cuda_commit_seg.zig,
cuda_kda_seg.zig, cuda_lanes_fill.zig, cuda_lanes_shared.zig, cuda_prompt_pieces.zig,
cuda_engine_shared.zig, cuda_engine_wait.zig, cuda_disk_ranks.zig and cuda_disk_image.zig
(the era's disk tier the segments write through), plus sample_cands.cuh and the glue
rows' per-row top-1. Every knob defaults off, so the pin's own paths run unchanged:
the lanes dispatch on together/multi, the shared verify goes through
cuda_engine_shared, and the engine opens only the knobs that are set.

Pin adaptations, each forced by a shape the pin does not have: the era's
`checkpoint_digest` field is restored on Engine (cuda_native and cuda_ranks read it);
`split_min` and `e.head` are dropped or mapped to the pin's `e.mtp`; Plan.size takes
the pin's `shared` argument; Arena.ptr is an accessor; `blankAs` and `seal` are added to
cuda_snapshots from the era source (with ringHolds) and re-exported on Engine; Link
gains `from`; marksOf keeps the pin's KV-share signature, so multiFill carries its own
keeps array. The 3-way merge left stray conflict markers inside cuda_follow.zig, which
were the real cause of a cascade of phantom struct errors - they are removed.

Gates on pin+0001..0023: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new (17 comment blocks collapsed),
fatbins green.
